Naturally I think this is cool because I proposed it too a while back! :)
I like the old AD&D monks. At high levels they had names like:
"Master of Flowers"
"Master of Dragons"
"Master of Spring"
etc.
To rise above a certain level (was it 15th?) you had to find and defeat a monk
of one higher level than you in non-fatal (unarmed?) combat, since there were a
limited number of each level of monk. There was only one Grand Master. This
could be worked into the quest - The start level would be just right too.

I also liked their really obscure abilities like: fall from n distance without
taking damage if within x of a wall (pits, trap doors etc in NH).

I can't remember much about them anymore. Any old AD&D fans out there who can
contribute a few ideas?
